          "entradaId": "freeman-601",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Amos 8:6. Neal may be rendered either “shoe” or “sandal.” From the form of expression here used the meanest, cheapest kind of sandal is evidently meant the poor debtor was sold into slavery because he could not pay for so small a matter as a pair of sandals. A similar mo…",
        "traduccion": {
