      "c-3a57495427abf91e": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-602",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Henderson’s translation gives the sense of the passage more clearly than the authorized version. He renders it: “They stretch themselves upon pledged garments close to every altar, and drink the wine of the amerced in the house of their gods.” The text refers to the unjust habits…",
